	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["210125560737B35B"]
			description: [
				"Congratulations on making it to &8ULV&r!"
				"The &6Steam Age&r acts as a tutorial for some key &bGregTech&r mechanics before you dive head first into electricity. "
				"It includes fluid and (possibly) item logistics, an introduction to ore processing, interdimensional travel, further processing of materials, and culminates in creating &7Electronic Circuits.&r"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&8i dont actually know if the steam age is supposed to be called \"ulv\""
				"&8but?"
				"&8i dont care."
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1
				id: "gtceu:bronze_hammer"
				tag: {
					Damage: 0
					DisallowContainerItem: 0b
					GT.Behaviours: { }
					GT.Tool: {
						DefaultEnchantments: [ ]
						HarvestLevel: 2
						MaxDamage: 191
						ToolSpeed: 7.0f
					}
					HideFlags: 2
				}
			}
			id: "01AE5BA787DA2A64"
			size: 3.0d
			subtitle: "\"This is where the fun begins.\""
			tasks: [{
				id: "47109C6BF4336776"
				title: "Welcome to ULV/Steam"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: -4.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["03603AED6CDBC2F0"]
			description: [
				"Progressing in the Steam Age would be difficult without producing steam, so lets start on that."
				""
				"You have three options for your first steam. No matter which one you choose, they all automatically push steam out of every side of the block, except for the bottom face."
				""
				"Also, be sure to fill them with water &cbefore&r turning the heat up, or the boiler will &4explode&r. This can be done by filling them using water buckets for the time being."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The &0Solid Boiler&r can take any furnace fuels, most likely &0Coal or Charcoal&r, and turns it into steam. It's steam production amount is low, but it is the simplest one to get up and running. It's also the &6cheapest&r to craft."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The &6Liquid Boiler&r can burn either &6Creosote&r (a liquid obtained from the Coke Oven multiblock detailed in a few quests) or &6Lava&r, and turns it into steam. This one is more expensive than the &0Solid Boiler&r, and is more difficult to keep running consistently, but it has the highest amount of steam production of anything you can make at this point."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The &bSolar Boiler&r does not require a fuel source, instead using the heat from the &eSun&r to produce steam. This one is the easiest to keep running, as it just requires passive water, but it is the most expensive option (requiring &7Silver&r) and only works during the daytime."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"All of these are valid options, choose whichever you like. The latter two require &bGlass Blocks&r, which require further infrastructure to make. However, there might be a way to make \"crude\" Glass Blocks as a substitute? "
			]
			id: "5C4AB4A662495496"
			subtitle: "WE BOIL"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "4B5FD189D8E05434"
					item: "gtceu:lp_steam_solid_boiler"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "1CA7AB1DEAD2D8D5"
					item: "gtceu:lp_steam_liquid_boiler"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "77E96CD73566BA78"
					item: "gtceu:lp_steam_solar_boiler"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Initial Power Generation"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5C4AB4A662495496"]
			description: [
				"Now that you have some Steam being made, you need something to use it on."
				"Steam machines can be powered by directly piping Steam into their inventory, but using Steam also requires them to have ventilation ports. &6Make sure these machines have a space to breathe&r, otherwise they will run a single recipe and then sit there doing nothing."
			]
			id: "0AB5B9343BC201BE"
			size: 1.25d
			subtitle: "NOW we're talking!"
			tasks: [{
				id: "387D18538B4E06C2"
				item: "gtceu:bronze_machine_casing"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Your First Machines"
			x: 0.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"0AB5B9343BC201BE"
				"0783BCEAC051BCF9"
			]
			description: ["The Extractor... extracts things. You'll need this later on to create Rubber, and the electric versions can turn materials into their fluid form."]
			id: "3944AAE13C38AB7C"
			subtitle: "Extracting your first Rubber"
			tasks: [{
				id: "34717C1F1DFEE3BD"
				item: "gtceu:lp_steam_extractor"
