			}]
			x: 2.5d
			y: 2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3F58D481792D21C9"]
			description: ["The Fluid Regulator, similar to the Robot Arm, can more precisely control fluids when used as a cover on inventories. Also similar to Robot Arms, they require the appropriate &cCirucits"]
			id: "2740F0B216E0C938"
			optional: true
			tasks: [{
				id: "6B2C611540B41CF2"
				item: "ulvcovm:ulv_fluid_regulator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 3.5d
			y: 4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3F58D481792D21C9"]
			description: ["Robot Arms have the same throughput as their equivalent Conveyors, but have additional limiting and monitoring options when used on inventories. They also require &cCircuits&r, which, depending on when you do these quests, you may not have access to yet."]
			id: "764C26E839BEEE09"
			optional: true
			tasks: [{
				id: "50CD77DD86F29332"
				item: "ulvcovm:ulv_robot_arm"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 3.5d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["27C583BEDD47FC27"]
			description: [
				"Pipes and covers are great, but what ties this system together is what else is on offer."
				""
				"There are a variety of other types of covers that can be made later in the game that perform specific actions. Covers that emit a &4Redstone&r signal based on the contents of a machine, covers that can &cfilter&r items and fluids,  covers that can &egenerate power&r or even &9resources&r &8(just water i think)&r, or even covers that add &6additional storage slots&r to a machine. Most of them are not accessible at the moment, but check them out in the next few tiers!"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Also, facades can be made by combining any given solid block and an Iron Plate in a crafting grid. This can be used to aesthetically hide or mask pipes or even entire machines. My favorite use of this is to create Glass Facades that add a transparent screen over the top of pipes. "
			]
			icon: "gtceu:storage_cover"
			id: "58004C9EC5A34BF3"
			tasks: [{
				id: "02D8A84F4B5BAF03"
				title: "sick"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Other features of Covers"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["03603AED6CDBC2F0"]
			description: [
				"The &6Coke Oven&r is likely to be your first Multiblock. It can turn Logs into &0Charcoal&r (did you figure out that you couldnt do this before?) and &0Coal&r into &8Coal Coke&r. &8Coke&r and the &6Creosote&r byproduct of this multiblock are what we are most interested in."
				""
				"You could have actually built this thing back in the Stone age, but it's only truly relevant now. It becomes cheaper if you have an Alloy Smelter."
			]
			id: "18060E52503CF80B"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "WHAT."
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "4E5AAA520EDE6FDD"
					item: "gtceu:coke_oven"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					count: 25L
					id: "23627ABE769C5FC7"
					item: { Count: 25, id: "gtceu:coke_oven_bricks" }
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			x: 2.25d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["0EAC2D2D25B74790"]
			description: ["Building and constructing a &8Primitive Blast Furnace&r is something of a rite of passage for any &bGregTech&r player. This is your gateway into creating &8Steel&r. It is also likely to be your first major crafting project. This pack includes the \"hard\" recipe for Firebricks, so you will need plently of Clay, Gypsum, and Calcite, among other things. Those last two are ores found in ore veins, and you can also macerate vanilla Calcite blocks, which is preferred if you can locate some."]
			id: "45AD4B6A0B7DDAA6"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "I started blasting"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "416C102CAB4C42D5"
