		{
			dependencies: ["7A5EB1A0C12044F7"]
			description: [
				"You may have noticed the \"Low Pressure\" quality of the steam machines you've made up to this point. Low pressure does, in fact, imply the existence of high pressure in this case. With some steel and wrought iron, you can upgrade your existing singleblock machines to high pressure variants. These (generally)* consume twice the amount of steam, but also perform recipes twice as fast. Depending on how much longer you plan to be in the steam age, these might do less work for you than you might expect, but they are still direct upgrades nonetheless."
				""
				"As a note, the machines can be directly upgraded (they actually must be), but the high pressure boilers can only be made from scratch. "
				""
				"*the high pressure miner is a bit weird, check the tooltip"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:hp_steam_solid_boiler"
			id: "17A8876B8590CDB5"
			size: 1.5d
			tasks: [{
				id: "1D8D4E34C373B398"
				title: "High Pressure Machines"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 8.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7A5EB1A0C12044F7"]
			description: [
				"If you find yourself constantly topped off on steam, good job! You're playing the mod correctly. &min my opinion.&r "
				"You may want a way to store all of that steam so that you can use it later. Now that you have Steel, you can create a multiblock that has 1000 buckets of storage. "
				"The IO of this is a bit funky. It auto outputs whatever it contains when a hatch is facing downward, and cannot accept input through that hatch."
			]
			id: "4254C3FC5CDCC5E9"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1DFF159D847119FD"
				item: "gtceu:steel_tank_valve"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 6.5d
			y: 2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7A5EB1A0C12044F7"]
			description: [
				"An option for creating bulk amounts of Charcoal while your coke ovens are tied up making Coke. May not get alot of use, and cant be automated, but maybe you can find a use for it?"
				"&8this multi is kinda terrible when flint and steel literally needs steel so this might get a recipe change"
			]
			id: "36FE436468A5DD2F"
			tasks: [{
				id: "503400391E22B218"
				item: "gtceu:charcoal_pile_igniter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 5.5d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["0783BCEAC051BCF9"]
			description: [
				"An alloy of Iron and Nickel. Unless you create one of the Steam Multiblocks, you likely wont use it until the next tier."
				"It does however, make for a decent material for tools. Some of it stats are marginally better than Wrought Iron, while the others remain the same, but Invar tools come with enchantments such as Efficiency I."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: false
			id: "48BDB248C95C8C48"
			subtitle: "Fe2Ni"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5F49858B9513B964"
				item: "gtceu:invar_ingot"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 2.5d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["140D720919268B58"]
			description: ["Cupronickel is a simple alloy of Copper and Nickel (could have guessed that) which is used more in later tiers. At this point, it can be used to create item pipes that are twice as effective as Tin. "]
			id: "55BB462B029F2E58"
			optional: true
			tasks: [{
				id: "59E77DD407D2ECE2"
				item: "gtceu:cupronickel_normal_item_pipe"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: -3.5d
			y: 4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["27C583BEDD47FC27"]
			description: [
				"Pipes come in two flavors, Item Pipes and Fluid Pipes. Other than the thing that they transport, though, they are very similar. &cThey both have a maximum throughput detailed in the item tooltip.&r Pipes have varying sizes, which further dictates this figure. "
				""
				"They also have different capabilities in regards to what they can carry. For example, &6Wooden Fluid Pipes&r are very cheap to make, but have the lowest throughput of any pipe and have a pitiful heat tolerance. Not great for transporting Steam, but useful for &9Water&r."
				""
				"Pipes automatically connect to blocks and other pipes that they are placed onto, and you can further configure them with a Wrench, as well as restrict the movement of the resources inside by shit clicking the edges."
			]
			id: "140D720919268B58"
			tasks: [{
				id: "29DE8EA6B61FCB49"
				title: "Pipes"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: -1.5d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7A5EB1A0C12044F7"]
			description: [
				"Steel grants you the opportunity to upgrade your tools. Steel tools have higher durability than anything else, and are also the first tools with Diamond mining level."
				""
				"The GregTech tool system rewards exploration of the materials that they can be made out of. This pack does not include any other tools from other mods to encourage you to experiment with this. Some materials are better at certain things, or like Invar tools, have unique perks like enchantments. "
				""
				"If you want to be lazy, the best material of the main tier metals that you have access to (steel, aluminum, etc) make for &ogood&r tools, but they are generally not the best that you can make. For example, in LV, you can create Diamond tools, which have better durability and mining speed than Steel."
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1
				id: "gtceu:steel_wire_cutter"
				tag: {
					Damage: 0
					DisallowContainerItem: 0b
					GT.Behaviours: { }
					GT.Tool: {
						DefaultEnchantments: [ ]
						HarvestLevel: 3
						MaxDamage: 511
						ToolSpeed: 9.0f
					}
					HideFlags: 2
				}
			}
			id: "45FEAFFD8CB7D54D"
			tasks: [{
				id: "77DF025B6B3EA5B8"
				title: "tool upgrades"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 8.5d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7A5EB1A0C12044F7"]
			description: ["The Tool Belt allows you to store multiple different tools in a single slot, accessed via a radial menu. You can add more slots with the Belt Pouch item from the same mod, by adding it like an enchanted book in an anvil."]
			id: "7D0143F632BBE0B0"
			tasks: [{
				id: "43890C0BD5E8656B"
				item: "toolbelt:belt"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 9.5d
			y: 2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["01AE5BA787DA2A64"]
			description: [
				"You needed to create a Mortar to get to this point, now you will need an arsenal of tools to progress. You can make these out of Iron, &6Bronze&r, and &7Wrought Iron&r at this point, but &6Bronze&r is the worst option out of these due to poor durability, and &7Wrought Iron&r is a direct upgrade to Iron, so the choice should be obvious."
				""
				"The next pages detail how these tools are used."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The Hammer can be used to create plates at a 2:1 ratio of ingots to plates. It can be used in world to mute machine sounds."
				"Notably, this is the only tool (and probably the only thing in the entirety of GregTech) that only uses raw, unprocessed Ingots in the recipe. Can you exploit this somehow?"
				""
				"The File is used to create rods at a 1:1 ratio, among other things."
				""
				"The Wrench is used in some miscellaneous recipes, but is predominantly used to mine and configure machines and other GregTech blocks."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The Saw can be used to cut rods into bolts and also create Wood items (planks and sticks for example) at rates that you would expect from Vanilla Minecraft"
				""
				"The Screwdriver can be used to configure Machines in ways that a wrench does not."
				""
				"The Wirecutter is the tool used to mine Wire, as well as the tool used to craft wire at this point in the game."
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1
				id: "gtceu:bronze_wrench"
				tag: {
					Damage: 0
					DisallowContainerItem: 0b
					GT.Behaviours: {
