		{
			dependencies: ["45AD4B6A0B7DDAA6"]
			description: [
				"A quirk of GregTech multiblocks is Wallsharing. This is the concept of having more than one multiblock use the same physical blocks as part of their construction. This can save on materials and allow for more compact setups."
				""
				"This can be done with any multiblock in the game, and hatches can also be shared once you create multiblocks with hatches. However, sharing power hatches (or steam hatches for the steam multiblocks) is potentially ill advised due to limitations of how much power those hatches can consume, and maintainance hatches are outright unable to be wallshared. Otherwise, go wild."
				""
				"A good use of this is saving materials and space on the Coke Oven and PBF. You can fit 4 of these multiblocks into a 5x5 footprint on the ground. Can you figure out how?"
				"&8editors note: fact check the maintainance hatch bit"
			]
			id: "6E6FD716E70B98B3"
			subtitle: "squis."
			tasks: [{
				id: "4224BE7E6D605556"
				title: "Wallsharing"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 6.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7A5EB1A0C12044F7"]
			description: ["Molds can shape materials into predefined shapes. The base mold is made with four steel ingots, and the shape is determined by arbitrary crafting recipes using the base mold. The Ball Mold from this quest is the only one required at the moment, but more will be needed in the future. A couple are still otherwise useful to you right now though, check out your options!"]
